<title>UK: Burton Group shares squeezed higher.</title>
<headline>Burton Group shares squeezed higher.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in retailer Burton Group Plc defied a weaker market on Monday and pushed higher as market-makers found themselves short of stock, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;They've been so depressed recently that they were due a bounce, and a few market makers got caught short this morning,&quot; one market maker said. &quot;The volume is fairly low but the price has been squeezed up.&quot;</p>
<p>Burton shares were 3-3/4p higher at 132-1/4 by 1155 GMT in volume of 1.3 million.</p>
<p>The shares are due to drop out of the FTSE 100 index from next Monday.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Marshall, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
